lib/crypto-algorithms (git submodule)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------

Author: Brad Conte (brad AT bradconte.com)
Upstream: https://github.com/B-Con/crypto-algorithms

Released into the public domain free of any restrictions. The author
requests acknowledgement if the code is used but does not require it; this
entry is that acknowledgement. Provided free of any liability and without
any quality claims by the author.

Only sha256.c is compiled into this library. The submodule is not
distributed inside this repository -- a clone gets it from upstream -- but
it is part of any build, so it is named here.

Upstream states these are not cryptographically secure implementations and
have no resistance to side-channel attacks. That is a property of the
SHA-256 underneath mqttCheckKey()'s HMAC, and worth weighing against a
threat model that includes an attacker who can measure the device. HMAC's
proof assumes a compression function that behaves; it says nothing about
how long that function takes to run.
